    kuna `condfold`, now on by default: Ghidra's ruleBlockOr folds `A || B` only
    when the block holding B prints at most a bare test; condfold also takes a
    sibling that prints a short statement prefix, rendered as a comma operand,
    within condstmts' budget.  Default on, a block that branches back to a block
    dominating it (a loop test) is never folded, so a do-while keeps its
    condition (regionstructure-loop-refine checks that shape).

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality", option `condfold off|on|wide`.

